# Frontend (micro-frontends) Docker build only needs services/micro-frontends,
# packages/design-tokens + packages/shared-utils + packages/itunda-pay-widget, and
# root workspace config -- NOT packages/saronite (2.5GB, React Native mini-apps,
# irrelevant to any web build) or any native mobile/backend tree. Mirrors the root
# .dockerignore's own real reasoning (see its own header comment) for the backend
# build, adapted for what a frontend build actually needs.
#
# services/api-gateway is NOT excluded (real bug hit building this, 2026-08-19):
# it's a real root package.json workspaces member (36KB, trivially cheap to keep) --
# excluding its source made `yarn install --immutable` think that workspace had been
# deleted and want to rewrite yarn.lock to drop it, which --immutable then refuses to
# do silently, so the build failed with "The lockfile would have been modified by
# this install, which is explicitly forbidden" even though nothing about this
# frontend build actually touches api-gateway's own code.
android
ios
services/backend
services/microservices
packages/saronite
docs
infra
.git
.claude
dump.rdb
**/build
**/.gradle
**/*.apk
**/*.ipa
**/node_modules
**/dist
